/Alt (A side-by-side panel chart. The left-hand panel shows broad equity market indices for Australia, the euro area, Japan, Korea, the United Kingdom, the United States and Taiwan, while the right-hand panel shows technology sector equity indices for the same economies. All series are indexed to 100 on 1 January 2026, allowing comparison of cumulative price movements across countries. Global equity prices have generally increased over 2026, although performance has differed across markets. Technology sector equities have been more volatile than broader equity indices and have generally recorded larger price movements, particularly in the United States, Taiwan and Korea, reflecting the greater importance of technology-related firms in these markets. Overall, the chart highlights that technology stocks have been a significant driver of equity market performance during 2026 and have experienced larger gains and drawdowns than broader equity markets.)
/K 11
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
